# HEY-CAPSULE-PACK PATCH 0025 (REMOVABLE): make `cargo test` compile again.
#
# Patches 0010/0018 (iroh 0.96 -> 1.0.2) and 0023 (GossipState::new gained a
# data_dir arg) updated every PRODUCTION call site and missed the two in-file
# #[cfg(test)] ones. The install only ever runs `cargo build`, so nothing caught
# it: `cargo test -p elastos-server` has not compiled since the iroh upgrade,
# which means the upstream suite could not validate any of our patches.
#
# Three mechanical fixes, mirroring the production shapes exactly:
#   Endpoint::builder()          -> Endpoint::builder(iroh::endpoint::presets::N0)
#   endpoint.address_lookup().add(..) -> if let Ok(al) = .. { al.add(..) }
#   GossipState::new(5 args)     -> + the data_dir arg
#
# After this, 50 of the 51 carrier tests pass. The one failure,
# test_remote_carrier_browser_exit_stream_relays_bytes_between_runtimes, is a
# two-runtime QUIC relay test that fails with "endpoint driver future was
# dropped"; it is NOT touched by this patch and is either an iroh 1.0
# behavioural change or an artifact of a sandbox with no real networking.
# Unresolved on purpose rather than silently ignored.
#
# KILL CONDITION: drop when the iroh patches are dropped (upstream on 1.x), or
# when upstream updates these call sites itself.
